english_text:
In the narration of Al-Sakuni from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq {a.s}
from his father, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir {a.s}, that he said:
"The hand of a thief is not to be cut off during a year of drought."

Sa'd ibn Tarif narrated from Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir {a.s}
who said: "Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib {a.s} ordered the cutting off of a hand for stealing an
iron helmet and for a shield that weighed thirty-eight ratl (a unit of weight)."

In the narration of Al-Sakuni from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq {a.s}
from his father, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir {a.s}, it is reported:
"Indeed, Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib {a.s} crucified a man in Al-Hirah for three days. Then on
the fourth day, Imam {a.s} took him down, prayed over him, and buried him."

Al-Hasan ibn Mahbub narrated from Abd Al-Rahman ibn Al-Hajjaj, who said:
I heard Ibn Abi Layla say, "In the pre-Islamic era, the blood money (diyyah) was one
hundred camels, and the Messenger of Allah {SWT} (peace be upon him and his family)
affirmed it. Then he imposed on the people of cattle two hundred cows, on the people
of sheep one thousand sheep, and on the people of garments one hundred garments."
Abd Al-Rahman said: ‘I asked Abu Abdullah {a.s} about what Ibn Abi Layla narrated, and
Imam {a.s} said: “Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib {a.s} used to say:
'The blood money is one thousand dinars, and the value of a dinar is ten dirhams.
For the people of gold, it is one thousand dinars;
for the people of silver, it is ten thousand dirhams;
for the people of the cities, it is ten thousand;
for the people of the deserts, the blood money is one hundred camels;
and for the people of the villages, it is two hundred cows or one thousand sheep.'"

It was narrated by Muhammad ibn Ismaʿil ibn Buzayʿ from Ṣalih ibn Uqbah
from Sulayman ibn Ṣalih from Abu Abdullah {a.s} who said:
"Indeed, for the sperm-drop (nutfah) there is a compensation of twenty dinars,
for the clot (Alaqah) forty dinars,
for the lump of flesh (muḍghah) sixty dinars,
for the bone (Aẓm) eighty dinars,
and when it is clothed with flesh, it is one hundred dinars.
Then it remains one hundred until it lets out a cry (at birth), and when it lets out a cry,
the full blood money (diyyah) becomes due."

Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated from Al-Thumali, from Sa'id ibn Al-Musayyab,
from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said:
"If a man strikes another man with a whip, Allah {SWT} will strike him with a whip of fire."

Saif ibn Umayrah narrated from Abu Bakr Al-Hadrami from Abu Abdullah {a.s}
who said: "Ibn Abbas used to say: Indeed, the One who counted the grains of sand in
Alij surely knows that the shares (of inheritance) do not exceed six."

Ibn Mahbub narrated from Ali ibn Riʾab from Abu Ubaydah from Abu Jafar {a.s}
who was asked about a paternal cousin and a grandfather (regarding inheritance).
Imam {a.s} said: "The entire inheritance belongs to the grandfather."

The Prophet {saws} said;
“The wretched one is he who is destined for wretchedness while in his mother's
womb.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“O’ Allah {SWT}, bless my nation in its (utilizing) early mornings on its Saturdays and
Thursdays.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Gatherings are based on trust.” (referring to that which is said and heard during
gatherings)

The Prophet {saws} said;
“If (even) a mountain were to oppress another mountain, Allah {SWT} would crush it to
dust.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom, and indeed, some speech has a magical
effect.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One (Allah {SWT}) in the heavens will show
mercy to you.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“It is not permissible for a believer to abandon his believing brother for more than three
days.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Whoever does not show mercy (to others) will not be shown mercy (by Allah {SWT} in
the Hereafter).”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“He does not (rightfully) thank Allah {SWT}, who does not thank people.” (for doing good
onto him)

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Throw dust onto the faces of those who excessively praise (you).” (advises rejecting
excessive flattery)

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Repel affliction with supplication.” (emphasizes the power of supplication (dua) in
warding off difficulties and hardships)

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Hearts are naturally inclined to love those who do good to them and to dislike those
who harm them.”

The Prophet {saws} said;
“There is no charity while a close relative is in need.” (needy relatives have a bigger
right over the money that was to be given in charity elsewhere)

The Prophet {saws} said;
“Health and free time are two neglected blessings.”
(failing to recognize the true value of good health and downtime or spare time)

The Prophet {saws} said;
“A man's gift to his wife increases her chastity.”
(strengthens her sense of loyalty and affinity for her husband)
